{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master","id":1502122,"title":"How long does it (on average) take to become a (multi) master?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-04T12:34:16-08:00","id":1502122,"title":"How long does it (on average) take to become a (multi) master?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> The template on the Core book, is for a mage with some months of training, passing from 3 Arcana dots to 6, and getting some Order skills (rotes, High Speech, Occult dot, Order Status). On 1st edition becoming a powerful mage was difficult as stats were exponential, but with the changes on second edition experience is linear (even if it is a lot when counting beats).<br /> <br /> <i>On average:</i><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>How long does it take for a Mage to become a Master of a Ruling Arcana?</li> <li>How long does it take for a Mage to become a Second Degree Master of their Ruling Arcana?</li> <li>Assuming a Legacy, how long to have Third Degree Ruling Arcana mastery?</li> <li>Assuming a Legacy, how long to reach 4th-5th Degree on the Legacy?</li> <li><b>Mechanically</b>, a starting Acanthus has the <b>potential </b>to learn faster from the start: Exceptional Luck Praxis with reasonable Gnosis (3) + Fate (3) + Willpower, can give multiple long lasting conditions that grant beats. <b>In game, does it make sense too to go for lost of beneficial conditions ASAP?</b></li> </ol>Thanks for the time and attention,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T12:47:42-08:00","id":1502125,"title":"","content":"Do you mean in lore or in game time?<br /> <br /> Lorewise, it's greatly up to your setting (just like the total number of mages etc.) But my impression based off of the stories of published NPCs is that gaining a dot of Gnosis takes on average 10 years, with more precocious mages (like the Nemean?) averaging closer to 5 years. And others being more like 20.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer masters to be rare and aloof, with the assumption that most mages never reach mastery in even one arcanum. Just as most professionals would never reach 5 dots in the skill they practice every day for decades.<br /> <br /> Though for PCs it depends entirely on how liberal you are with allowing advancements and the timescale of your stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:01:34-08:00","id":1502128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502125#post1502125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean in lore or in game time?<br /> <br /> Lorewise, it's greatly up to your setting (just like the total number of mages etc.) But my impression based off of the stories of published NPCs is that gaining a dot of Gnosis takes on average 10 years, with more precocious mages (like the Nemean?) averaging closer to 5 years. And others being more like 20.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer masters to be rare and aloof, with the assumption that most mages never reach mastery in even one arcanum. Just as most professionals would never reach 5 dots in the skill they practice every day for decades.<br /> <br /> Though for PCs it depends entirely on how liberal you are with allowing advancements and the timescale of your stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore AND game time (but Lore mainly).<br /> <br /> I am just making these calculations for the example.<br /> <br /> Any new player can have 3 Gnosis and 3 Arcana (ruling) from character creation, this can be done as representing some months training. A natural prodigy or encouraged to focus on specific things, etc.<br /> <br /> IF that character in particular is an Acanthus, they have the option of making Exceptional Luck a Praxis AND spending willpower and using High Speech / Any other Yantra for a bigger dice pool that on average will net them Exceptional successes, so they can recover their Willpower point AND gain a condition that grants beats PLUS the effects of the spell (also picking conditions, which will grant beats with the Exceptional Success)*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I might be misreading the Boons / Exceptional Success part of the Core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Casting the Spell p. 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Success: The spell\u2019s effect takes place better than<br /> imagined.<b> The character regains one spent point of Willpower,<br /> and the player may choose one of the following results</b>;<br /> \u2022 A bonus step in the primary spell factor.<br /> <br /> \u2022 A Reach in the primary spell factor.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 A Condition which will give Arcane Beats when resolved,<br /> on either the mage or her subject.</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 All Mana spent on the spell is refunded, and the mage<br /> receives one more point of Mana.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The spell ignores any Withstand levels and takes effect at<br /> full Potency.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boons p.134</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grant a number of beneficial Conditions (such as Charmed,<br /> Informed, Inspired, or Steadfast) equal to Potency for the<br /> Duration of the spell. None of these Conditions grant<br /> Beats when the subject resolves them (<b>unless the caster<br /> achieved an exceptional success in the casting</b>)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand here that the Condition from achieving an Exceptional Success is distinct from any Fate granted conditions which only grant beats IF you got an exceptional success, adding to the on benefit of exceptional success not replacing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:03:19-08:00","id":1502140,"title":"","content":"As was pointed out in the question thread since you can only gain 1 beat per scene via resolving conditions, there is little gained from giving yourself more conditions via Exceptional luck as opposed to just casting any praxis and gaining exceptional success in every scene...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:03:37-08:00","id":1502141,"title":"","content":"The XP system on it's own is not a good guide; it's very abstract and above all, makes no allowance for time, or indeed downtime.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, there are a bunch of assumptions that the setting seems to be written with that aren't made explicit, and may even not be realised by the writers.<br /> <br /> Like, becoming a master is clearly meant to be a big deal. It's rare in the NPCs, and the setting explicitly gives masters a special place in the Pentacle by giving them voting rights in convocations... But, at the same time, for most starting characters, it's two dots away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:14:14-08:00","id":1502143,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember you can only get one Beat from resolving conditions per scene. (I'm actually not sure if you can get both a regular and an Arcane Beat from conditions in one scene?)<br /> <br /> Also any mage can take a Dramatic Failure on a spellcasting roll to get an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> I also think it's important to remember that the game mechanics are meant to model stories about mages, especially the exceptional success and beat rules. Rather than model the way mages actually grow in power within the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:49:17-08:00","id":1502156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502143#post1502143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember you can only get one Beat from resolving conditions per scene. (<b>I'm actually not sure if you can get both a regular and an Arcane Beat from conditions in one scene?)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems so each one is an independent category, so I would say you can AS LONG ONE OF THE CONDITIONS IS NOT FROM SPELLCASTING.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beats p. 81</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Any time you resolve a Condition, take a Beat\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane Beats p. 83</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022<b>Any time you resolve a Condition resulting from spellcasting, Paradox, or a magical effect, take an Arcane Beat<br /> instead of a normal one.</b> Letting a spell causing a Condition expire does not count as resolving it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But then my example of using Exceptional Luck to get two conditions does not work as both Conditions come from spellcasting, so only a single Arcane beat can be earned per scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502143#post1502143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also any mage can take a Dramatic Failure on a spellcasting roll to get an Arcane Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I had forgotten this part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-04-2023, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:53:43-08:00","id":1502159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502141#post1502141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The XP system on it's own is not a good guide; it's very abstract and above all, makes no allowance for time, or indeed downtime.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, there are a bunch of assumptions that the setting seems to be written with that aren't made explicit, and may even not be realised by the writers.<br /> <br /> Like, becoming a master is clearly meant to be a big deal. It's rare in the NPCs, and the setting explicitly gives masters a special place in the Pentacle by giving them voting rights in convocations... But, at the same time, for most starting characters, it's two dots away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not two dots. The lowest Gnosis a master can be in 5. Gnosis caps your highest Arcana rating and the second highest, so double masters require Gnosis 6.<br /> <br /> That is more than double the XP of two dots in a ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> Lorewise, for a mage who intends to develop 4/5 Arcana work of likely be slower, perhaps starting out with 2/2/1/1 or 2/1/1/1/1 dots in their starting Arcana, and slowly build all 4/5 up to Gnosis limits before even increasing their Gnosis (3/2/2/2/2 is 5 dots in Arcana before you need to buy Gnosis 2).<br /> <br /> So, while this is described mechanically the opposite extreme, i could imagine any multiple master being a lots slower...<br /> <br /> Of course lorewise, most NPCs don't spend all of their time and XP on Arcana and Gnosis dots. They have families* and freinds*, and careers (even if it they start working for an order) so spend XP on order status, and merits, and skills and attributes which they can actually use in their mundane life.<br /> <br /> *The shadow name merit protects their family and friends from being hit by their long term nimbuses, which is a big part of the lore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T20:31:57-08:00","id":1502178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502128#post1502128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand here that the Condition from achieving an Exceptional Success is distinct from any Fate granted conditions which only grant beats IF you got an exceptional success, adding to the on benefit of exceptional success not replacing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that Conditions granted by a spell only grant Beats from their resolution if they're negative, and the exception described under Fate's Boons section is linking &quot;you can grant positive Conditions with the standardized Fate spell mechanics,&quot; &quot;unlike normal positive Conditions, where it is merely inadvisable to resolve them before getting a Beat from a negative Condition due to the per-scene limit, positive Conditions granted by spells do not provide Beats when resolved,&quot; and &quot;if you roll an exceptional success on a spellcasting roll, you can apply a Condition that grants an Arcane Beat when resolved.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is no extra Beat being provided, and in the case of a spell designed to apply multiple positive Conditions you would pick the one whose resolution will grant an Arcane Beat and proceed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T04:41:39-08:00","id":1502194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502159#post1502159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not two dots. The lowest Gnosis a master can be in 5. Gnosis caps your highest Arcana rating and the second highest, so double masters require Gnosis 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Though, I still think that becoming a Master is XP-wise, a lot easier than the Lore implies, if we take the simple number of XP required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course lorewise, most NPCs don't spend all of their time and XP on Arcana and Gnosis dots. They have families* and freinds*, and careers (even if it they start working for an order) so spend XP on order status, and merits, and skills and attributes which they can actually use in their mundane life. </div> </div> </div>I disagree there. Lorewise, NPCs just don't use XP at all. They're supposed to be fictional people, and people don't operate in the manner that XP systems do. I'd keep in mind that even PCs don't (generally) spend XP, the player spends the XP to change their character.<br /> <br /> That's before we get into the zero-sum nature of the XP system. Like, a lot of NPC mages have high mundane stats because it makes narrative sense that they would have picked up such skills along the way; but that's not the way the system works. Any XP spent on mundane skills, is not being spent on magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:27:45-08:00","id":1502843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502194#post1502194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. Though, I still think that becoming a Master is XP-wise, a lot easier than the Lore implies, if we take the simple number of XP required.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> What do you think an in-game average for PCs is right? An in-game year for first mastery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T11:31:07-08:00","id":1502860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502122-how-long-does-it-on-average-take-to-become-a-multi-master?p=1502843#post1502843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think an in-game average for PCs is right? An in-game year for first mastery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't know. It'll depend how you break up sessions; plus how knowledgeable of the system your players are, as well as how generous you are as a ST.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've not had a game where the players reached master, but then I've made it much harder to gain arcana/gnosis*, and my players have tended to be very relaxed about pushing the system to get XP.<br /> <br /> *Just as an aside, I split the XP system so that Arcana and Gnosis required just arcane XP. I believe I wanted to encourage developing mundane skills as well as arcane ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}